From d5a7c1b840e1123361eafbbf8852e438f92145d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: timothyc012 <timothyc012@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 14:12:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(build): use automatic JSX runtime for the library build
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The root tsconfig compiled JSX with the classic runtime, so files
without an explicit React import (CanvasShapeRenderer.tsx) emitted
bare React.createElement calls into dist. Any consumer without a
global React crashed with 'React is not defined' the first time a
shape body rendered. tsconfig.types.json and the rollup externals
already assumed react/jsx-runtime — align the JS build with them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dist/canvas-react.js | 2636 ++++++++++++++++++++++--------------------
 tsconfig.json        |    2 +-
 2 files changed, 1372 insertions(+), 1266 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dist/canvas-react.js b/dist/canvas-react.js
index 668ff60..b05f9c3 100644
--- a/dist/canvas-react.js
